manifest.json.lock

# Per-run extraction output stays on disk and out of the repository. manifest.json
# beside this file is the durable evidence: it carries each run's model, temperature,
# rules fingerprint, counts and grounding stats, which is where every figure the paper
# cites came from.
#
# The tradeoff, stated so nobody discovers it later: summarise.py also opens the run
# folders, for the cross-draw entity-overlap figure ("found by all five", load_run at
# line 138). That part of the summary works on a machine that has the folders and not
# on a fresh clone -- re-run run_variability.py to regenerate them. Everything derived
# from the manifest alone, which is the headline governance and variance result, needs
# nothing but this directory.
*/run_*/
